  "title": "THINGS-EEG2: A large and rich EEG dataset for modeling human visual object recognition",
  "description": "THINGS-EEG2 is a large EEG dataset from 10 participants who viewed 16,540 training images and 200 repeated test images from the THINGS database. Images were shown in a rapid serial visual presentation stream at 5 Hz across four sessions per subject. Resting-state recordings are also included. The dataset is intended for modeling human visual object recognition and for building encoding models.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded with a BrainVision actiCHamp system at 1000 Hz with 63 channels in a 10-10 layout and an online band-pass filter of 0.01-100 Hz. Each of the four sessions per subject had 5 training runs, 1 test run, and 2 resting-state runs. Catch trials required a button press.",
